Feature: Payment Authorization and Order Status Consistency
  As an e-commerce customer
  I want my order status to accurately reflect the outcome of my payment authorization
  So that I am never charged, or shown as confirmed, for a payment that did not succeed

  Background:
    Given a customer has a cart ready for checkout
    And the payment gateway is configured with sandbox test bank credentials

  @smoke @critical @risk-critical
  Scenario: Order is confirmed only after successful authorization and capture
    Given the customer submits payment with a valid test card
    When the gateway returns a successful authorization and capture response
    Then the order status is "confirmed" in the order-service API response
    And the order status in the database matches "confirmed"

  @negative @risk-critical
  Scenario: Order remains marked as payment failed when the gateway declines authorization
    Given the customer submits payment with a test card configured to trigger a decline
    When the gateway returns a decline response
    Then the order status is "payment failed" in the order-service API response
    And the order status in the database matches "payment failed"

