Feature: CVV and Card Data Protection
  As an e-commerce customer
  I want my CVV and card data to never be exposed
  So that my payment information remains secure and compliant with PCI-DSS

  Background:
    Given a customer is on the checkout page with a card payment form

  @smoke @security @risk-high
  Scenario: CVV is masked in the UI after entry
    Given the customer enters a CVV into the payment form
    When the CVV field loses focus
    Then the UI displays the CVV as masked characters only

  @negative @risk-high
  Scenario: Checkout rejects payment when CVV format is invalid
    Given the customer enters a CVV with an invalid format
    When the customer submits the payment
    Then the checkout displays a validation error requesting a valid CVV
    And the payment request is not sent to the gateway

  @regression @security @data-driven @risk-high
  Scenario Outline: CVV is absent from logs and error responses across failure scenarios
    Given a payment attempt results in "<failure_type>"
    When the failure response is captured
    Then the CVV is absent from the network log entry
    And the CVV is absent from "<expected>"

    Examples:
      | failure_type    | expected                  |
      | invalid CVV     | the error-message payload |
      | gateway timeout  | the error-message payload |
      | gateway decline  | the error-message payload |

