Feature: Idempotent Payment Retry
  As an e-commerce customer
  I want a retried payment after a network timeout to not charge me twice
  So that I am not double-billed for a single order

  Background:
    Given a customer initiates a payment with a generated idempotency key

  @regression @risk-high
  Scenario: Duplicate debit is prevented when payment is retried with the same idempotency key after a timeout
    Given the initial payment request times out before a gateway response is received
    When the customer's client resends the identical payment request with the same idempotency key
    Then exactly one capture is recorded for the order
    And no duplicate debit is recorded against the customer's account

  @negative @risk-high
  Scenario: Payment request without an idempotency key is rejected before reaching the gateway
    Given the customer's payment request is missing an idempotency key
    When the request is submitted for processing
    Then the request is rejected with a validation error
    And no authorization attempt is sent to the gateway

