Feature: Stock Validation During Checkout
  As an e-commerce customer
  I want checkout to prevent overselling when stock runs out during payment
  So that I am not charged for an item that is no longer available

  Background:
    Given a product listed at checkout has a tracked stock level

  @regression @risk-medium
  Scenario: Authorization is rolled back when stock depletes to zero before capture
    Given the product stock reaches zero via a concurrent sandbox transaction while the customer's authorization is in-flight
    When the checkout attempts to proceed to capture
    Then the order is blocked or rolled back before capture
    And the order status reflects "stock unavailable"

  @negative @risk-medium
  Scenario: Customer sees an out-of-stock error after concurrent stock depletion
    Given the product stock has been depleted by a concurrent transaction
    When the customer attempts to complete checkout for that product
    Then the checkout displays an out-of-stock error
    And no payment authorization is initiated

  @boundary @edge-case @risk-medium
  Scenario: Two concurrent checkouts contend for the last unit of stock
    Given the product stock level is exactly 1 unit
    When two customers submit checkout for that product at the same time
    Then only one checkout proceeds to payment authorization
    And the other checkout is shown an out-of-stock error before payment

