Feature: Promo-Adjusted Amount Consistency
  As an e-commerce customer
  I want the amount authorized and settled to match my promo-adjusted cart total exactly
  So that I am charged the correct amount after a discount is applied

  Background:
    Given a customer has a cart with a promo code applied

  @regression @data-driven @risk-medium
  Scenario Outline: Cart total, authorization amount, and settlement amount match across promo types
    Given the cart total reflects a "<promo_type>" promo code
    When the payment is authorized and settled
    Then the authorization amount equals the cart total
    And the settlement amount equals "<expected>"

    Examples:
      | promo_type | expected                     |
      | percentage | the discounted cart total     |
      | flat       | the discounted cart total     |
      | expired    | the original, undiscounted cart total |

  @negative @risk-medium
  Scenario: Expired promo code is rejected and cart total reverts to original price
    Given the customer applies a promo code that has expired
    When the cart re-evaluates the promo code
    Then the cart displays an expired-promo error
    And the cart total reverts to the original, undiscounted price